#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Wave 37: Little Hands, Just Three, an Eighth Time — the eighth 3-only wave.

Wave 36's honest assessment named this wave the same way waves
29-35 named theirs: the age-3 gap (142 against 160 at age 4, gap
18) "closes only by more waves of this kind, at honest quality,
or not at all." Seven consecutive 3-only waves have narrowed it
102 -> 90 -> 78 -> 66 -> 54 -> 42 -> 30 -> 18. This is the
eighth: twelve more records banded 3-3, built to the rules waves
30-36 proved — short (<= 20 minutes), adult-led, big pieces, one
rule per game, the adult as a player — because the band is honest
for the same reason: these are three-year-old moments (a plant
given a drink and a promise on Earth Day, a rainbow found standing
in a sprinkler's mist, a bear rocked to sleep on a circle's hum),
and age 4, holding 160 records, does not miss them.

Measured before this wave (primary category = categories[0],
records covering age 3): holidays and team-community were the
floor at 11 each; seasons / stem / icebreakers / outdoor 12
each; crafts 13, pe-movement 13, music-rhythm 13; quiet-focus
16, rainy-day 17. Music-rhythm and rainy-day are now tied as
the thinnest primary categories on the whole shelf (38 each),
and music's age-3 count (13) sits well below rainy-day's (17) —
so the pack repeats the proven shape exactly: one record for
every one of the 11 categories — the floor rises 11 -> 12
everywhere — plus a second music-rhythm record. Result,
asserted in the wave log: age 3 142 -> 154, age 4 unchanged at
160, the headline gap 18 -> 6, narrowed for the eighth wave
running. Tag deltas: Earth Day 6 -> 7 (a floor holiday tag
rises), summer 31 -> 32 (the thinnest season rises).

The drama/coding lane, recorded not padded (standing rule):
there is still no drama or coding category in the archive's
eleven, and no tag in the validator's vocabulary names one.
This wave does not invent a twelfth category to look complete,
and it does not stretch a cloud-naming or an echo drum into a
'drama' or 'coding' label it is not. The lane stays on the
record as an honest gap until a wave is briefed to build it
properly, with its own category, its own shelf, and records
written for it first.

Near-duplicate screen: token Jaccard >= 0.55 against every
existing name+tagline is asserted below and fails the run.
Closest deliberate neighbours, kept on purpose:
- big-earth-day-first-garden-promise vs planting records on
  the older shelf (seed journals, garden maths): nothing is
  measured or journalled here — ONE plant is given a drink and
  a promise, and the keeping of the promise across the week is
  the record.
- big-sprinkler-rainbow-edge-walk vs water-play records for
  older kids (sprinkler obstacle runs, sponge relays): nobody
  runs and nothing is raced here — the group stands at the
  mist's edge, watches for the rainbow the mist sometimes
  keeps, and takes one slow walk through the edge, in turn.
- big-hide-the-bear-seek-together vs winter-hide-and-seek
  (5-10, children hide) and box-boat-row-along (3-5, found
  in the screen's neighbourhood): children never hide here —
  the BEAR hides, in places with a paw or an ear honestly
  showing, and the whole group seeks as one pack; an earlier
  draft of this slot WAS a box-boat record, and it was cut
  before running because box-boat-row-along already rows
  that boat at 3-5 — the pack does not re-skin a neighbour.
- big-cardboard-brick-wall-build vs nesting-cup-towers
  (3-5) and big-felt-quilt-wall-build (3-only, flat felt on
  a wall): nothing is nested and nothing is stuck flat here —
  a free-standing wall is engineered course by course, its
  lean read as information, its fall reported as data, and
  its rebuild changed by the evidence. (An earlier draft of
  this slot was a ramp-roll record; cardboard-ramp-roll-lab
  already covers letting-go at 3-5, so it was cut too.)
- big-laundry-line-helping-hands vs dressing-frame and peg
  records on the fine-motor shelf (worked solo, at a table):
  the frames there are furniture; the line here is a job —
  two carriers, one cloth, a real line, pegged by its own
  carriers, because the room's pretend washing needed doing.
- big-mirror-face-copy-my-face vs Simon Says and copy-the-
  leader games on the icebreaker shelf (commands, outs,
  winners): nobody is out and nothing is commanded here —
  one face is made, one partner copies it, and a copy that
  wanders is received as a new face worth copying back.
- big-cloud-lying-picture-names vs weather-watch records
  (charts, symbols, forecasts): nothing is recorded here —
  the group lies down, looks up, and names what one cloud is
  being today; the naming is the whole record, and a cloud
  that changes its mind mid-name is the lesson.
- big-water-painting-fence-picture vs painting records with
  real paint (mixing, drying, keeping): the paint here is
  water and the picture is supposed to disappear — that
  vanishing IS the record, and it is why the fence can hold
  a hundred pictures a morning.
- big-belly-buddy-breathing-watch vs quiet-time and story-
  rest records (eyes closed, adult-led, longer): nobody is
  asked to sleep or to close their eyes here — a soft buddy
  rides the belly, the breath moves it, and watching the
  buddy ride is a job a three-year-old can actually do.
- big-beach-ball-keep-it-floating vs balloon-tennis and
  ball-passing records (nets, scores, faster hands): nothing
  is scored and there is no net — one big soft ball is tapped
  gently UP by a seated circle, and its falling is met with
  the record's one line: down is where it rests, not loses.
- big-echo-drum-one-hit-back vs rhythm-pattern records on
  the music shelf (sequences, notation, clapped patterns):
  no pattern is kept here — the adult hits ONCE, the circle
  hits once back, and the listening between the two hits is
  the entire instrument.
- big-humming-lullaby-bear-sleep vs singing records (words,
  verses, performances): there are no words here at all —
  one soft tune, hummed by the whole circle, rocks one bear
  to sleep, and the quiet after the last hum is the ending.

Safety notes are practical only — no medical claims anywhere.

Run once: dedupes by id, writes data/activities.json + collections.json.
Run scripts/build.py afterwards.
"""
