      safety="The plant is non-toxic and checked leaf by leaf before the session; nothing from it is food and the session says so once, plainly. Water lives in cups, half-full, carried in two hands at walking pace: the only floods in this record are small ones, and the adult's towel is already on the floor beside the pot before the first pour — spilled water on a hard floor is the session's one real hazard and it is mopped the moment it lands, every time, without ceremony. Stones are palm-sized or bigger, washed, smooth, and checked for cracks before they come out; they are placed, never thrown or mouthed, and any stone small enough to argue with a mouth never joins the set. Soil stays in the pot: hands that have touched soil are washed when the circle rises, as garden hands are.",
