      ["one big soft bear (the hider — big enough that a good hiding place still leaves a paw, an ear, or a hopeful nose showing; soft, washed, and famous: this bear has a name and the room knows it)", "the whole room, arranged as the hunting ground (its ordinary furniture, with the adult's one addition: nothing is hidden IN anything that closes, locks, or tips)"],
